    "parent": "llm-v2c4-fresh-news-dev-run-20261114",
    "question": "Do pairwise comparisons of the de-identified seven-day text dossiers of two assets of the same week, made by two analyst agents and, where they disagree, an adjudicator, who name the asset whose reports give the better price outlook over the next seven days, carry information on the next-week return rank beyond the existing quant forecast, the price controls and the attention counts, on the 104 test weeks 2023-01-06 to 2024-12-27? The comparison score of an asset and week is its Bradley-Terry strength over the decided comparisons of the week; an asset without a dossier takes the neutral score 0. Gate: weekly OLS coefficient of the within-week rank of the comparison score in a regression of the within-week return rank on an intercept and the ranks of the quant forecast, the price controls and three attention controls (seven-day linked documents, dossier lines, dossier present); Newey-West t (lag 4) of the mean weekly coefficient at least 2.0 with a positive mean over at least 78 weeks, and a positive mean in 2023 and in 2024.",
    "reuse": "exploratory",
